# Ignore rules for the suite. The rule that matters most is the first one:
# deployment state and secrets must be un-committable, not merely
# "remember not to commit them", because this project's whole security story
# rests on private keys that never leave their owner's machine.

# ── secrets and per-host configuration ──────────────────────────────────────
# .env is generated by install_ubuntu22.sh / start_macos.sh with a fresh
# POPOPX_ADMIN_TOKEN. .env.example is the checked-in template and the only
# .env-shaped file that belongs in git.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
keyring/
official_keys/
.popopx-keyring

# ── runtime state ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The SQLite database, which holds the channel Ed25519 identity and epoch keys
# alongside the ledger and the session secrets. Losing it means every
# zero-knowledge channel this suite created stops being readable, so these are
# ignored to prevent BOTH accidental commits and accidental `git clean`.
.data/
data/
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# ── local dev scratch ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
.run/
*.log
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/

# ── editor and OS noise ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
._*
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# ── internal brief, not shipped source ──────────────────────────────────────
# prompt.md is the spec the suite was built from. It stays on disk for
# reference but is not part of the deliverable.
prompt.md
